            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0173" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">467n11/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-04T18:00:00+02:00">September 4, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 5—12:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Consular corps today requested High Commissioner to take into consideration the
                    question of indemnification for damages suffered by foreigners as a result of
                    the recent disturbances and to inform it of the procedure to be followed in the
                    verification of the damages and in the presentation of claims.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
